Package: ltsp-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         debootstrap,
         squashfs-tools,
         gettext-base,
         lsb-release,
         debconf-utils,
         openssh-client,
         python3
Recommends: nbd-server,
            tftpd-hpa,
            dnsmasq | isc-dhcp-server,
            nfs-kernel-server,
            xinetd
Suggests: python3-gi,
          gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
          freerdp3-x11 | remmina
Description: LTSP6 thin client server tools
 ltsp-build-client, ltsp-config, ltsp-chroot, ltsp-info and related
 server-side tools for building and managing LTSP (Linux Terminal
 Server Project) thin-client chroot images, plus the NBD root/swap
 servers used to serve them over the network.
 .
 ltsp-support opens a support session on a client: it lists the
 clients that have booted, asks the user there for consent, and shows
 that screen over an ssh port forward. It is a GTK3 program, so it
 needs python3-gi and an RDP client to watch with, which is why both
 are suggested.
 .
 This package also ships example configs and documentation for
 running an HAProxy + keepalived high-availability RDP load balancer
 in front of a pool of xrdp servers (see
 /usr/share/doc/ltsp-server/examples/).

Package: ltsp-app
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         x11-xserver-utils,
         x11-utils
Breaks: xfdesktop4 (<< 4.20.2-2~ltsp13+1)
Description: LTSP6 pieces for the xrdp application servers
 What the desktop sessions on an LTSP application server need beyond
 Debian's own packages.
 .
 ltsp-primary-left makes the leftmost monitor of a multi-monitor RDP
 session its primary one, so files saved to the desktop appear on the
 monitor that carries the panel.
 .
 It requires the xfdesktop4 from the LTSP archive, which renders
 backdrops at the size a monitor has once xorgxrdp has split the
 session into the client's monitors, and moves every icon dragged to
 another monitor rather than only the first.

Package: ltsp-client-core
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
